 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "Nonhalting and PA-independence for a 196-state Turing machine",
  "excerpt": "PA196 is an explicit binary Turing machine that searches for a contradiction in ordinary first-order Peano arithmetic (PA). Lean 4 proves that it runs forever from a blank tape and that PA proves neither its exact arithmetic halting sentence nor its negation."
 },
